Hi Managers,

Thanks to the handful of people who responded, who suggested checking 
various different things:

Martin Andersen:
Check in rc.config for any NTP configuration different to that in ntp.conf

Douglas Stephens:
Make sure that the upstream servers are actually version 1, and to check out 
www.ntp.org

Florian Heigl:
To check the output from ntpdate -v -d time_server


All of things were useful in tracking down the issue, but the problem 
appears to be that xntpd was being confused by NAT on our firewall, such 
that replies weren't getting processed correctly. I set up ntpd on a 
separate box which didn't need any address translation, then got the Tru64 
boxes to point to this, and everything has now synchronised.

Regards,

Rob


